A||||17||Shiner||Confessions of a good mechanic gone bad||||6||
Z||000000||Shiner||09-06-2000||10:42 PM||||Did any of you ever intentionally try to break you Craftsman tools, just to see if you could?  That lifetime warranty really eggs me on.||||reg||6
Z||000001||HugGRRRFiero||09-06-2000||11:07 PM||||Doesn't it though?  Michigan winters up here freeze bolts real good.<P>I'm always saying "Come on Baby...&lt;CRACK&gt; eeww ya!" every time I'm yank'in on one of those 4' breaker bars on the end of a 1/2" Socket wrench.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">  <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||09-06-2000||11:15 PM||||When ever my wimpy body cant provide enough power to break those bolts loose, I just grab the handle out of the floor jack to use with that 1/4 inch rachet. Yes, Sears knows me on a first name basis!||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||09-06-2000||11:31 PM||||Besides that fact that I'm a wimp, I use cheater bars at the least little excuse, because they give me more control.  You can gradually apply increasing amounts of torque, until that stubborn fastener finally breaks loose - and if something breaks, I'd much rather have it be the lifetime Craftsman tool than the fastener head, or my hand!<P>The people at Sears are great - they <B>never</B> ask for explanations, they just replace the tool I broke, and send me away with a smile  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> .  <BR>   ||||reg||14
Z||000004||gixxer||09-07-2000||12:51 AM||||Buy Snap-On tools if possible. They just don't break. At least I haven't broken any, and most of my Snap-on metric sockets are about 20 years old. And I don't have to worry about mangling my hands up if a tool breaks.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||09-07-2000||02:07 AM||||I love craftsman!! I broke what must have been a 10 year old ratchet at work, and they gave me a brand new one right off the shelf, no questions.  Now that's customer service!<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 150,000 miles and counting!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">    <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker||||reg||1
Z||000006||whamel||09-07-2000||09:04 AM||||Heck, I buy broken craftsman tools from the local pawn shop all the time!  Whenever the guys gets something in broken he gives me a ring.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>And I have had the guy ask me 'off the record' once what happened, but he just seemed curious about hearing the story of how you can snap a breaker bar in half while warping it in the middle.<BR>Wade||||reg||1
Z||000007||bHooper||09-07-2000||09:23 AM||||i had a 10 yo torx socket... for the seatbelts/brakes.  i snapped it off taking the calipers off, returned it, no questions asked.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000008||DJRice||09-07-2000||12:19 PM||||They have replaced several 1/4", 3/8", and 1/2" rachet handles for my father and I.  <P>And torx bits, pliers, screwdrivers, and even a 15 year old torque wrench. (which still worked, but the plate with the measurements had popped off).<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||1
Z||000009||fierospeeder||09-07-2000||02:36 PM||||I also take my sears 3 ton floor jack's handle to use it as a pipe to increase my torque on a ratchet.<P>I just got my sears credit card, and its 10% sale this week, im turning my garage into a shop and buying a drill press, shop vac, grinder and a steel workbench which went on sale for this month for 110 bucks.<P>The only sears tool that broke on me so far is my 1/4" ratchet, it still works but the ratcheting part seems stripped on the inside.||||reg||1
Z||000010||ThatRickGuy||09-07-2000||04:15 PM||||I have a broken craftsman tool, and as soon as I get the fiero going so I can drive to sears I'll get it replaced. it's a 1/2 inch socket extension, but instead of just having that little spring pushed ball, it has a little 'flipper-flapper' that holds the socket on. well, the flipper flapper broke, so now to get sockets on and off I have to stick a screwdriver into it.||||reg||1
Z||000011||webbee||09-07-2000||06:28 PM||||I don't break much of their stuff, but when I do, back it goes. Have you noticed that the quality of the new stuff isn't as good? Socketts aren't cut as deep, walls are thiner, not as hard. That's progress I guess!?!||||reg||1
Z||000012||rockcrawl||09-07-2000||09:11 PM||||When my screwdrivers start to get rounded off, I clamp the tips in a vice and give them a quick 'snap' so I can get some shiney new ones.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||Gokart||09-07-2000||09:42 PM||||Hopefully they'll be just as cheary and helpful when I bring back the piece of s*it Crapsman buffer/polisher I bought 5 months ago. Went to use it for only the 3rd time last weekend and it s*it the bed <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">. Can't find the box nor the receipt!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Gokart_sig_1.gif"> <P>Marc                     87GT||||reg||13
Z||000014||DjKid||09-07-2000||09:54 PM||||That lifetime warranty, that they are so proud of..... is only on handtools...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000015||Shiner||09-08-2000||12:47 AM||||Wow, I didn't think THIS many people are as evil as I<BR>"Dad, I'm going to get a torque wrench at Sears"<BR>"Is it an EVIL torque wrench? *pinky to mouth*"<P> I put a heck of a lot of heat on my 3/8'ths ratchet, and I am just WAITING for this sucker to break.  Damn thing sheared SIX, YES SIX bolts on the front bumper and didn't show anything in the way of wear.  I was really hoping it would just shred to pieces and I could take a fun little trip to Sears, but no.  ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Raydar||09-08-2000||01:55 AM||||I broke the last 3/4 inch off of my BFSD (screwdriver) trying to get my @!$!#!* front bearing/hub assembly out of the steering knuckle. (Was rusted and "crudded" into place.) <P>Also (different project) shot the bearings in my electric drill. It really didn't like being used as a grinder.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 09-08-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||ChadMan||09-08-2000||09:34 AM||||When I got married my best friends chipped in and bought me a great Sears gas grill and Craftsman grill tools.  The tools have the same red, blue and clear hand grips that Craftsman hand tools have, but they are engraved with the following message:<P>"NOT GUARANTEED FOREVER - CONSIDERED A KITCHEN UTENSIL"||||reg||10
